<title>USA: Former Electric Boat workers get gov't funds.</title>
<headline>Former Electric Boat workers get gov't funds.</headline>
<dateline>GROTON, Conn. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Labor will give $4.3 million in job relocation assistance to 957 Electric Boat Corp workers who are being laid off this year, Connecticut's two U.S. senators said on Friday.</p>
<p>Submarine-maker Electric Boat is a subsidiary of General Dynamics Corp.</p>
<p>Of the 957 workers, 539 were laid off in February, while the remaining 418 will be terminated later this year, a spokesperson for Senator Christopher Dodd (D) said.</p>
<p>Electric Boat has already said it expects to cut 1,500 jobs this year because of a shrinking workload.</p>
</text>
